---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const sections = [
  { id: "who-we-are", title: "Who we are" },
  { id: "scope", title: "Our role" },
  { id: "applicants", title: "For job applicants" },
  { id: "information-we-collect", title: "Information we collect" },
  { id: "how-we-use-information", title: "How we use information" },
  { id: "subprocessors", title: "Sharing and subprocessors" },
  { id: "international-transfers", title: "International transfers" },
  { id: "retention", title: "How long we keep information" },
  { id: "security", title: "Security" },
  { id: "your-rights", title: "Your rights" },
  { id: "cookies", title: "Cookies" },
  { id: "children", title: "Children" },
  { id: "changes", title: "Changes to this policy" },
  { id: "contact", title: "Contact" },
] as const;
---

<LegalLayout
  document="privacy"
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Emploist handles personal data: what we collect, how AI ranking and AI assistants use job applications, who we share data with, and your rights."
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Emploist is an applicant tracking system for businesses, with hosted careers pages and optional AI ranking of
    applications. It's operated by Navaneeth CT, an individual based in India ("Emploist", "we", "us").
  </p>
  <p>
    This policy explains how we handle personal data when you use the Emploist app, including through an AI assistant
    you connect to it, apply for a job on a careers page that runs on Emploist, visit emploist.com, or contact us. You
    can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="scope">2. Our role</h2>
  <p>
    Companies that use Emploist ("customers" or "employers") put their own content into it, such as jobs and comments,
    and receive applications through it. Together with the match scores and other records Emploist creates from them,
    this is "Customer Data", as our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> define it. Each customer controls its Customer Data, and
    we process it on the customer's behalf under our <a href="/terms/#data-processing">data processing terms</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We're the controller of the personal data we use to run Emploist ourselves: team members' account details, the
    invitations we send, AI assistant connections, billing records, support emails, security logs, and data about
    visitors to our website. This policy mainly covers that data.
  </p>

  <h2 id="applicants">3. For job applicants</h2>
  <p>
    If you applied for a job through a careers page that runs on Emploist, the employer whose page it is controls your
    application. It decides what the form asks, who sees your application, whether AI is used, and how long your
    application is kept. Please read the employer's privacy notice, and contact the employer with questions or requests
    about your application. If you contact us instead, we'll refer you to the employer or pass your request on to it. Your email is
    stored in our support inbox, which Google hosts.
  </p>
  <p>For the employer, Emploist:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      stores your name, email address, resume, answers to the employer's questions, and your application's stage and
      history, and makes them available to the employer's team
    </li>
    <li>
      sends the emails the employer sets up, for example when you apply or your application moves to a new stage, through
      our email provider
    </li>
    <li>
      if the employer has AI ranking on, sends the text of your resume, your answers (except phone numbers), and the job's
      details to our AI provider, TypeSafe AI, Inc., in the United States, to score how well your application matches
      the job. The score helps the employer decide which applications to review first. It doesn't reject, advance, or
      email you by itself. People on the employer's team make the decisions.
    </li>
    <li>
      sends your application to AI assistants, such as Claude or ChatGPT, that people on the employer's team connect to
      Emploist, when they ask for it. These assistants are run by companies the employer's team chooses, under terms the
      employer or its team members agreed with them.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When you visit a careers page or apply, our servers also record technical data, such as your IP address and browser
    details, in request logs. We control these logs and use them to keep Emploist working and secure.
  </p>

  <h2 id="information-we-collect">4. Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account information.</strong> Your name and email address, which you give us or which we get from Google
      or Microsoft if you sign in with them. You need to give us these to use Emploist.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your work in Emploist.</strong> What you do for your company, such as the jobs you create, your comments,
      and the applications you move, including through AI assistants you connect, is stored with your name and is
      visible to your teammates. It's part of your company's Customer Data.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Invitations.</strong> When an admin invites someone, we store the invited person's email address, their
      role, and who invited them, and email them an invitation.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>AI assistant connections.</strong> If you connect an AI assistant, we store which assistant you allowed,
      its details, and the tokens that let it work for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing.</strong> Dodo Payments sells our plan and handles payment details, and we never see your full
      card number. We send Dodo the email address of the admin who first checks out and the company's name, and we get
      the plan's status and payment records from Dodo. We also keep a record of who has used a free trial.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical information.</strong> When you sign in, we keep a session record with your IP address and
      browser details. Our servers keep request logs with IP addresses, browser details, and the addresses of the pages
      and data requested, which can include details from Customer Data, such as a search term. We use Customer Data in
      our logs only to provide, secure, and support Emploist, as our data processing terms describe.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Support.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email address, your message, and anything you include.
      Cloudflare forwards these emails to our support inbox, which Google hosts (Gmail).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Website visitors.</strong> emploist.com has no analytics, forms, or third-party scripts. Its host receives
      standard request data, such as your IP address and browser details. Some of our pages, such as our <a href="/listed-on/">Listed on</a>
      page, show badges from the directories that list Emploist. The badges load from those directories' websites, so the
      directories also receive this request data when you open those pages, and handle it under their own privacy
      policies.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="google-microsoft">Google and Microsoft sign-in</h3>
  <p>
    If you sign in with Google or Microsoft, we receive your name, email address, account ID, and sign-in tokens, and
    from Google, a link to your profile picture. We only ask for basic profile access, not access to your email, files,
    or anything else in your account. Microsoft sign-in also asks to keep that basic access over time, so Microsoft
    gives us a long-lived token. We use this data only to sign you in and to show your name and email address in
    Emploist, including to your teammates and the AI assistants they connect. We keep it with your account until you
    delete your account, and we don't sell it, use it for advertising, or share it except as this policy describes. You
    can remove Emploist's access in your Google or Microsoft account settings.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-information">5. How we use information</h2>
  <p>
    We use personal data only for these purposes. If you're in the European Economic Area (EEA) or the UK, the table also
    shows the legal basis we rely on.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Purpose</th>
        <th>Legal basis</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>
          Providing Emploist: running accounts and companies, careers pages, the emails customers set up, and the AI
          assistants people connect
        </td>
        <td>
          Legitimate interests in providing the service your company signed up for, or our contract with you if you're
          personally a party to it
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Signing you in and keeping Emploist secure, including preventing spam and abuse</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests in keeping Emploist and the people who use it safe</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Billing with Dodo, tracking AI credits, and preventing repeat free trials</td>
        <td>
          Legitimate interests in running the plan and keeping the tax and accounting records the law requires
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Answering your questions and requests</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests in helping the people who use Emploist</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Service emails, such as sign-in codes, invitations, and important notices about Emploist</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests in signing people in and keeping customers informed</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          Finding and fixing problems, keeping Emploist and our website working, and improving Emploist using aggregated
          or de-identified usage information
        </td>
        <td>Legitimate interests in running Emploist well</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Complying with the law, enforcing our Terms, and handling legal claims</td>
        <td>
          Legal obligations under EU or UK law, where they apply, and otherwise legitimate interests in complying with the
          law and protecting our rights
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    We don't sell personal data, use it for advertising, or send marketing emails. We don't use Customer Data to train
    AI models. We don't make decisions about you based solely on automated processing that have legal or similarly
    significant effects on you.
  </p>

  <h3 id="right-to-object">Your right to object</h3>
  <p>
    <strong
      >If you're in the EEA or the UK, you can object at any time, on grounds relating to your situation, to our use of
      your personal data based on legitimate interests.</strong
    > To object, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>. We'll then stop, unless we have
    compelling legitimate grounds that override your interests, rights, and freedoms, or we need the data for legal claims.
  </p>

  <h2 id="subprocessors">6. Sharing and subprocessors</h2>

  <h3>Subprocessors</h3>
  <p>
    These providers process personal data for us to run Emploist. For Customer Data, they're our subprocessors, and this
    is the list that our <a href="/terms/#data-processing">data processing terms</a> refer to.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Provider</th>
        <th>What it does</th>
        <th>Location</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>OVHcloud</td>
        <td>Hosting the app's servers and database</td>
        <td>Singapore</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Cloudflare, Inc.</td>
        <td>Storing files and database backups, DNS, delivering logos, and forwarding email sent to our support address</td>
        <td>Asia-Pacific (file storage) and worldwide</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>TypeSafe AI, Inc.</td>
        <td>AI ranking of applications, for companies that have it on</td>
        <td>United States</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Resend (Plus Five Five, Inc.)</td>
        <td>Sending emails</td>
        <td>Japan and the United States</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p id="about-typesafe">
    TypeSafe's terms say it won't use the data we send to train its AI models. They let it keep and use that data for
    its own purposes, such as preventing fraud and abuse, complying with the law, and service telemetry. See
    TypeSafe's <a href="https://typesafe.ai/legal/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> and <a
      href="https://typesafe.ai/legal/data-processing">data processing addendum</a
    >.
  </p>
  <p>
    We'll update this list before we add or replace a subprocessor, and tell customers as our data processing terms
    describe. Our website, emploist.com, is hosted by Vercel, which receives website visitors' request data, but not data
    in the Emploist app.
  </p>

  <h3>Other recipients</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Dodo Payments</strong> (<a href="https://dodopayments.com/legal/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>), the
      merchant of record for our plan, which uses the billing details described above under its own privacy policy.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong> (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>) and <strong>Microsoft</strong
      > (<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">privacy statement</a>), if you sign in with them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong>, which hosts our support inbox (Gmail) under its own terms and <a
        href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a
      >, not a data processing agreement. It stores the emails people send us, and our replies come from a Gmail
      address. If you're a customer, don't include applicants' details in emails to us. Refer to jobs and applications
      by their addresses in Emploist instead, without search terms in them, such as an applicant's name.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>AI assistants</strong> that you or your teammates connect. We send an assistant the data it asks for, which
      can include your name, email address, and role, and your company's Customer Data. Each assistant is run by a
      company that you or your company choose, such as Anthropic or OpenAI, under its own terms. It isn't our
      subprocessor, and we don't control what it receives.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your company.</strong> Your teammates can see your name, email address, and activity in Emploist.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Professional advisers</strong>, such as lawyers and accountants, who must keep it confidential.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authorities and others</strong>, when the law requires it, or when it's needed to protect the rights,
      safety, or security of the people who use Emploist, the public, or Emploist.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A successor</strong>, if Emploist's business is transferred, for example to a company set up to run it or
      to a buyer.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="international-transfers">7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Our servers are in Singapore, and our file storage is in the Asia-Pacific region. We access data from India, and some
    providers process it in other countries, including the United States and Japan, as the list above shows. Google may
    store our support inbox in its data centers worldwide.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you use Emploist or email us, you give your personal data to us directly, and we protect it as this policy
    describes. For Customer Data from the EEA, the UK, or Switzerland, our data processing terms include the European
    Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses. Where our providers' processing needs a transfer mechanism, we rely on the
    Standard Contractual Clauses, an adequacy decision such as the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, or another mechanism
    that data protection laws recognize. For our support inbox, we have no Standard Contractual Clauses with Google, and
    rely on Google LLC's certification under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, its UK Extension, and the Swiss-US Data
    Privacy Framework. You can ask us for a copy of these safeguards.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">8. How long we keep information</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Information</th>
        <th>How long we keep it</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Account information</td>
        <td>
          Until you delete your account, except your name, which we keep so that your comments and activity still show
          who did them.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Company information, invitations, and Customer Data</td>
        <td>
          Until an admin deletes the company, or we delete it under our <a href="/terms/#suspension-and-termination"
            >Terms</a
          >, for example after it has had no active Plan, as our Terms define it, for 12 months in a row.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Applicants' data</td>
        <td>
          The employer decides. When the employer deletes an application, job, or company, we delete it from our active
          systems. Copies in backups and logs are removed over time, and some details may remain in the employer's
          other records, such as notifications, until those are deleted.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>AI assistant connections</td>
        <td>Until you disconnect the assistant or delete your account.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Billing records</td>
        <td>
          Until the company is deleted, except records of who has used a free trial, which we keep to prevent repeat
          trials, and records the law requires us to keep.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Support emails</td>
        <td>As long as we need them to handle your request and any follow-up.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Logs and backups</td>
        <td>For a limited period, for security, troubleshooting, and recovery, then deleted or overwritten.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Data already sent to our providers or to AI assistants is kept under their own terms.</p>

  <h2 id="security">9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We protect personal data with reasonable measures, including encrypted connections (HTTPS), access
    controls so that, in the app, only a company's team and the AI assistants they connect can see its data, private
    storage for resumes,
    sign-in without passwords, and regular database backups. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects personal
    data we control, we'll notify you and the authorities as the law requires. If it affects Customer Data, we'll notify
    the customer, as our data processing terms describe.
  </p>

  <h2 id="your-rights">10. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal data, to get a copy
    of it in a portable format, to restrict or object to how we use it, to withdraw consent where we rely on it, and to
    complain to a data protection authority.
  </p>
  <p>
    To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>, ideally from the email
    address on your account. We may need to confirm your identity, and we'll respond within the time the law requires.
    You can also delete your account in Settings or, if you're no longer in a company, by emailing us. If you applied
    for a job, contact the employer about your application (see <a href="#applicants">For job applicants</a>).
  </p>

  <h3>EEA and UK</h3>
  <p>
    You can complain to the data protection authority where you live or work, or where you think an infringement
    happened. In the UK, that's the Information Commissioner's Office. You can also complain to us by email, and we'll
    acknowledge your complaint within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h3>India</h3>
  <p>
    You can review and correct the information you've given us, or withdraw consent you've given, by emailing us. If you
    withdraw consent or don't give us information we need, we may not be able to provide Emploist to you. You can raise
    any grievance with our Grievance Officer, Navaneeth CT, at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}
      >{SITE.supportEmail}</a
    >. As India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 comes into force, you'll also have the rights it gives.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cookies">11. Cookies</h2>
  <p>The Emploist app uses only these cookies, which are needed to sign you in:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Cookie</th>
        <th>What it does</th>
        <th>How long it lasts</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>__Secure-emploist.session_token</code></td>
        <td>Keeps you signed in</td>
        <td>7 days, renewed while you use the app</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>__Secure-emploist.state</code></td>
        <td>Protects your sign-in with Google or Microsoft</td>
        <td>5 minutes</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The app also uses your browser's local storage to remember your theme and whether the sidebar is collapsed. Emploist
    sets no cookies on careers pages or our website, and we don't use analytics, advertising, or tracking cookies. If an
    employer's careers page design loads content from other websites, those websites may receive your IP address and set
    their own cookies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">12. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Emploist is for businesses, and you must be 18 or older to use the app. We don't knowingly collect personal data
    from children as a controller. If you believe we have, email us and we'll delete it. Employers decide who can apply
    for their jobs, and are responsible for any consent the law requires for applicants under 18.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">13. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy, and we'll change the date at the top when we do. We'll email people with an Emploist
    account about material changes before they take effect.
  </p>
  <p>
    We publish this policy in English and translate it into other languages. If a translation differs from the English
    version, the English version applies, as far as the law allows.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions or requests, or to reach our Grievance Officer, Navaneeth CT, email <a
      href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a
    >. Emploist is operated by Navaneeth CT, an individual based in India, trading as Emploist.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
